        "5093627965c0d4a6bd8564f792dd8f221229ced6"
      ],
      "title": "test capture_from_stdin: fix checking whether is_gui",
      "message": "test capture_from_stdin: fix checking whether is_gui\n\nInvocations of check_capture_stdin() typically have cmd as a tuple of\n(executable, args...).  Checking for '-k' in the executable generally\nfails, unless the absolute path happens to include it[1].  Fix that by\nskipping cmd[0].\n\n[1] https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/22094#note_2955330495\n\nSigned-off-by: Alex Badea <alex.badea@keysight.com>\n",
      "author_name": "Alex Badea",
      "author_email": "alex.badea@keysight.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-12-15T11:48:48.000-08:00",
      "committer_name": "Alex Badea",
      "committer_email": "alex.badea@keysight.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-12-15T12:00:19.000-08:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/7e7837f2b6c255ced462d86bbf01abe3ec3376d3"
    },
    {
      "id": "5093627965c0d4a6bd8564f792dd8f221229ced6",
      "short_id": "50936279",
      "created_at": "2025-12-15T12:00:19.000-08:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "793229910311cb1212116a59769ea34d9941a7f9"
      ],
      "title": "test capture_from_stdin: scan stderr for capture started/stopped",
      "message": "test capture_from_stdin: scan stderr for capture started/stopped\n\nconsole_file() in wsutil/wslog.c determines whether a message goes to\nstderr or stdout based on its log level.  \"Capture started\" and \"Capture\nstopped\" as MESSAGE level, \"Wireshark is up and ready to go\" is INFO.\nAdjust the test to match.\n\nSigned-off-by: Alex Badea <alex.badea@keysight.com>\n",
      "author_name": "Alex Badea",
      "author_email": "alex.badea@keysight.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-12-15T11:57:47.000-08:00",
      "committer_name": "Alex Badea",
      "committer_email": "alex.badea@keysight.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-12-15T12:00:19.000-08:00",
